{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a61e39c4a1fabb79", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# NAVA: Native Audio-Visual Alignment for Generation\narXiv: 2605.30073\nAuthors: Longbin Ji∗\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose NAVA, a Native Audio-Visual Alignment framework that formulates joint audio-video generation as context-conditioned native audio-visual alignment to enable precise event-level correspondence modeling.\n  2. We introduce an Align-then-Fuse MMDiT architecture for modality-aware audio-video alignment and efficient collaborative denoising, alongside Timbre-in-Context Conditioning for flexible content-timbre binding.\n  3. Extensive experiments and user studies demonstrate that NAVA significantly outperforms representative baselines in audio-visual synchronization, semantic consistency, visual quality, and timbre controllability.\n\nTags: experiments, we propose, we introduce, extensive experiments", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "084bfb49-665f-4b6b-8d17-78ca4000b371", "uuid": "a0e96997-40bb-486e-99ff-1fbb52f901ea", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T17:06:22.129Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# NAVA: Native Audio-Visual Alignment for Generation\narXiv: 2605.30073\nAuthors: Longbin Ji∗\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose NAVA, a Native Audio-Visual Alignment framework that formulates joint audio-video generation as context-conditioned native audio-visual alignment to enable precise event-level correspondence modeling.\n  2. We introduce an Align-then-Fuse MMDiT architecture for modality-aware audio-video alignment and efficient collaborative denoising, alongside Timbre-in-Context Conditioning for flexible content-timbre binding.\n  3. Extensive experiments and user studies demonstrate that NAVA significantly outperforms representative baselines in audio-visual synchronization, semantic consistency, visual quality, and timbre controllability.\n\nTags: experiments, we propose, we introduce, extensive experiments", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
